IT Triage Logger

A simple Python-based IT triage logger designed to simulate the initial process of logging and prioritising IT support issues.

The program allows a user to enter an issue and provide a detailed description. It then uses basic keyword matching and conditional logic to assign an appropriate impact level and provide a response based on the priority.

Current Features

* Records the reported IT issue
* Records a detailed description of the problem
* Identifies common issues using keywords
* Assigns an impact level:
    * Low Impact
    * Medium Impact
    * High Impact
    * Emergency
* Provides a response based on the assigned priority
* Generates a simple summary of the user’s report

Purpose

This project was created as part of my self-directed learning in Python and IT support. It is designed to demonstrate how basic programming concepts can be applied to a realistic IT service desk scenario.